<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
    <h2>JavaScript async / await</h2>
    <p>Use of async and await enables the use of ordinary try / catch blocks around asynchronous code.</p>
    <p id="result"></p>
    
    <script>
        async function add(a,b){
            let response = await (a+b);
            display(response);
        }
        function display(a) {
            document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = a;
        }
        add(5,20);
    </script>

</body>

</html>